@@ -52,6 +52,13 @@ Only API callers use `GET /connect?token=...&interactions=answer|none`: it immed
 
 Authenticated shared HTTP requests pass through the `connection/request` waterfall before body transfer. A listener may refuse new requests or await `next()` through response completion; removing its owning fiber removes admission behavior. Desktop uses this hook to lock new API work during an approved installation without canceling already-admitted work. Client disconnection aborts the handler signal; the bridge stops socket writes and drains any remaining response chunks. WebSocket stream ownership remains with API Gateway.
 
+
+### Trusted proxy authentication
+
+Setting `trustedProxySecretFile` selects an exclusive alternative to browser sessions. The absolute path must name a private file containing 64 lowercase hex characters (32 random bytes), optionally followed by one newline. Connection reads it at activation and fails load for missing or malformed files. Each index, API request, and WebSocket upgrade must carry the exact `X-Dsh-Proxy-Secret` header; duplicate or malformed values are refused. Host, Origin, and Fetch Metadata checks still apply, including to index requests. The advertised URL has no token, no browser cookie is issued, and old cookies and launch tokens cannot authenticate requests.
+
+The TLS-terminating authenticating proxy must authorize every public route, remove client-supplied copies of the header, and inject its key only after authorization. Keep the backend inaccessible from the public network and unrelated local accounts. This shared key authenticates the proxy, not individual users: every admitted request acts as the operator. Store the key outside configuration dumps, command lines, logs, and build outputs; restart Connection and reload the proxy after rotation. Authentication is checked when a request or upgrade begins; it does not revoke an established stream. Static assets still require protection at the public proxy.
+
